  "family": "rock_punk",
  "lineage": "Celtic metal combines metal-band practice with selected Celtic musical material and instruments rather than one standardized ethnic sound. Cruachan’s Irish branch supplies the model here: electric guitars, bass and drums interact with tin-whistle and fiddle lines, with a harsh vocal layer. Keith Fay describes sustained folk/metal integration, while recording interviews document studio expansion with folk instruments and strings. This authored six-role reduction retains both acoustic melody instruments instead of substituting a generic synthesizer for them.",
